Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 18:03:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: qcom: scm: register the Gunyah watchdog on the
 Nothing Phone (1)

The firmware reports SMCCC v1.0, so arm_smccc_hypervisor_has_uuid() never
makes the vendor hypervisor UID call and the Gunyah watchdog device is not
registered, although the APSS watchdog is reserved for Gunyah and nothing
else can serve as a hardware watchdog. Register it on this machine anyway;
gunyah_wdt probes the watchdog status call and returns -ENODEV if the
hypervisor does not answer it.
---
 drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c | 14 +++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
index 4702ad898..1a0afa3cd 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
@@ -2494,9 +2494,17 @@ static void qcom_scm_gunyah_wdt_init(struct qcom_scm *scm)
 		"arm,sbsa-gwdt",
 	};
 
-	/* Bail out if we are not running under Gunyah */
-	if (!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_HAVE_ARM_SMCCC_DISCOVERY) ||
-	    !arm_smccc_hypervisor_has_uuid(&gunyah_uuid))
+	/*
+	 * Bail out if we are not running under Gunyah. Some boards run Gunyah
+	 * behind firmware that only reports SMCCC v1.0, so the hypervisor UID
+	 * call is never made and the check fails although the watchdog is
+	 * there (Nothing Phone (1): the APSS watchdog is reserved for Gunyah).
+	 * On those, register the device anyway: the driver probes the Gunyah
+	 * watchdog status call itself and backs off if it is not answered.
+	 */
+	if ((!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_HAVE_ARM_SMCCC_DISCOVERY) ||
+	     !arm_smccc_hypervisor_has_uuid(&gunyah_uuid)) &&
+	    !of_machine_is_compatible("nothing,spacewar"))
 		return;
 
 	/*
